[size=140][u]Rescue Rangers[/u][/size]

Your ships rescue the crews of your destroyed ships from space and bring them to a station, a "Dormitory" ship, or Stasis.

[size=130][u]Features[/u][/size]
[list]
[*] [b]Sector mode[/b] - the Rescue ship waits at its Home Station and covers the Home Sector and the sectors within its gate range.
[*] [b]Fleet support mode[/b] - with no Home Station set, the Rescue ship docks at its "Dormitory" ship and covers the sector it is in.
[*] [b]Mimic[/b] - fully supported in fleets.
[*] [b]Rescue priority[/b] - the nearest spacesuit first, or the one with the least oxygen left.
[*] [b]Several Rescue ships[/b] - can share one sector or overlapping ranges without chasing the same person.
[*] [b]Return them back on Replacement Ship[/b] - rescued crew is returned on the Replacement Ship of the ship they were lost from.
[*] [b]Keep rescued on board as crew[/b] - rescued people join the Rescue ship's crew right away.
[*] [b]Stasis[/b] - rescued people are kept on your stations or on space rented on NPC stations, instead of filling a "Dormitory" ship.
[*] [b]Overview[/b] - the [b]Rescue Rangers[/b] overview, opened from the top menu or the right-click menu of a Rescue ship, shows every Rescue ship, the rescue statistics, everyone rescued and each Rescue ship's settings.
[/list]
